// SoundFont: plays a melody through the built-in General MIDI bank.
// `soundfont(pattern, "gm", preset)` routes pattern events into the
// SF2 synth: gate, freq, and velocity are extracted from the events.
//
// Preset 0 is Acoustic Grand Piano in the GM standard. Preset 1 is Bright
// Acoustic Piano, layered an octave below for body.
//
// Gain staging: `soundfont()` and the reverbs (freeverb, dattorro) all output
// at unity. `out()` is pure summation across calls, so two layered voices +
// reverb chains will clip without explicit per-voice attenuation. Each chain
// here targets ~0.3 peak so the summed output stays under 1.0 with headroom.

bpm = 100

melody = n"c4 eb4 g4 c5 ~ g4 eb4 c4 d4 f#4 a4 d5 ~ a4 f#4 d4 eb4 g4 b4 eb5 ~ b4 g4@1.25 eb4@2 c4@1.75 ~@8"

// Lead piano: dry voice + small freeverb tail. 0.3 leaves headroom for the
// transient peaks that exceed the steady-state RMS by ~3x.
melody
    |> soundfont(@, "gm", 0) * 0.3
    |> @ + freeverb(@, 0.65, 0.4) * 0.15
    |> out(@)

// Sub-octave bright piano, delayed by a quarter beat for a layered feel.
// dattorro is fully wet, so we attenuate after the effect and add only a
// quiet dry blend (no doubled-amplitude `+@` trick from the old patch).
bass = melody |> transpose(@, -12).late(.25) |> soundfont(@, "gm", 1) * 0.22

dattorro(bass) * 0.6 + bass * 0.5 |> out(@)